From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 20:02:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07252/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5718: 3-arm retrieval
 A/B artifact -- no arm reliably wins

Live 3-arm A/B (Qwen3.5-9B-MTP, 24 inductions, GPU 1): none / static / retrieval.
Mean graded cell-recall: none 0.089 (one 0.71 lucky induction), retrieval 0.031
(max 0.218), static 0.003 (max 0.020). All pairwise deltas leave-one-out
outlier-fragile -> verdict no_reliable_signal_high_variance for both
retrieval-vs-none and retrieval-vs-static. Consistent with exp5717: injecting
playbook text does not beat no-injection on this floored/noisy offline metric.
Signal (unreliable at N=8/arm): retrieval degrades best-case induction LESS than
the static block (retrieval max 0.218 vs static 0.020), i.e. RAG >= fixed if
anything. The retrieval mechanism itself works (retrieves situation-relevant
patterns). Recommendation: do NOT graduate; keep both gates OFF.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
